arguments.content:
Two things on the pin, one of them a shipping blocker.

1. BLOCKER (implementation shape): the pin as tested is correct for the experiment but unbounded for production. One 4 KiB shadow page is held per (multi-node) chain until file close. At 60 fps with two submits per batch that is ~120 chains/s → 480 KB/s → 28.8 MB/min → ~1.73 GB/h, and this port's IOVA window is P7580_IOVA_SIZE = (4 GiB − P7580_IOVA_START) ≈ 4.06 GB (gem.h:71), so a long-lived compositor exhausts the IOVA space in roughly 2.4 hours even before the page-table-leaf and BO-struct memory is counted. Do not ship the pin as-is; KWin is exactly the workload it would kill.

   Production shape (from KbaseCompare, and it follows from this finding):
   - bounded per-file ring of N shadow pages, N=2–4;
   - reuse of slot k is gated on completion of the *consumer* submit (k+1), not on submit k's own fence — that is the rule the whole mechanism teaches;
   - with df->serial_prev ordering all submits of a file, one submit of slack is provable, so N=2 with a one-submit gate is safe; N=4 buys margin;
   - assert at reuse (slot index + generation) and at close (pages still held), the same discipline as the pin/unpin labels. A ring that silently grows is the same class of bug as the old lifetime.

2. Measurement attempt, honestly reported: I tried to size the chain rate from the live compositor and could not — the 30 s window I just captured was idle (0 "dispatch slot=", 0 "ioctl jc=", 0 shadow pins, and qmlscene6 was no longer running; kwin 4660 was resident with 11 fds but submitting nothing). So there is no measured chains/s figure from this window; the arithmetic above is KbaseCompare's estimate, and it needs an animated window to be validated. When you next have the animation up, a 30 s kwin-cap capture will give the pin count directly and settle the ring size (pins/30 s ⇒ pages/min).

The 30/30 PASS on #46 stands (that pass was uncontended in effect: zero foreign faults/timeouts in every window). Item 1 (STATUS-before-CLEAR) remains the only unlanded fix that gates status interpretation.

